"To find the value of \\( h(6) \\), we need to substitute \\( x = 6 \\) into the function \\( h(x) = \\sqrt{\\frac{x^3 + 72}{2}} + 1 \\).\n\nFirst, calculate \\( 6^3 \\):\n\\[ 6^3 = 216 \\]\n\nNext, add 72 to 216:\n\\[ 216 + 72 = 288 \\]\n\nThen, divide 288 by 2:\n\\[ \\frac{288}{2} = 144 \\]\n\nNow, take the square root of 144:\n\\[ \\sqrt{144} = 12 \\]\n\nFinally, add 1 to the result:\n\\[ 12 + 1 = 13 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( h(6) \\) is \\(\\boxed{13}\\)."
