"The sum of an infinite geometric series is given by the formula \\( S = \\frac{a}{1 - r} \\), where \\( a \\) is the first term and \\( r \\) is the common ratio. Given that the sum \\( S = 45 \\) and the common ratio \\( r = -\\frac{1}{2} \\), we can substitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[ 45 = \\frac{a}{1 - \\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\frac{a}{1 + \\frac{1}{2}} = \\frac{a}{\\frac{3}{2}} = \\frac{a \\cdot 2}{3} = \\frac{2a}{3} \\]\n\nTo find \\( a \\), we solve the equation:\n\n\\[ 45 = \\frac{2a}{3} \\]\n\\[ 45 \\cdot 3 = 2a \\]\n\\[ 135 = 2a \\]\n\\[ a = \\frac{135}{2} = 67.5 \\]\n\nTherefore, the first term of the series is \\(\\boxed{67.5}\\)."
