"First, we solve the system of equations:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n2x - 9y &= 14 \\\\\n6x &= 42 + y\n\\end{align*}\n\nSubtract the first equation from the second:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n6x - (2x - 9y) &= 42 + y - 14 \\\\\n8y &= 28 \\\\\ny &= 3\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, substitute $y = 3$ back into the first equation:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n2x - 9(3) &= 14 \\\\\n2x - 27 &= 14 \\\\\n2x &= 41 \\\\\nx &= 20.5\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we find the product $xy$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\nxy &= 20.5 \\cdot 3 \\\\\nxy &= 61.5\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the value of the product $xy$ is $\\boxed{61.5}$."
