"To find the value of \\( x + y \\) in the sequence \\( 243, 81, x, y, 3, \\ldots \\), we need to determine the common ratio \\( r \\) of the geometric sequence.\n\nFirst, we calculate the common ratio \\( r \\):\n\\[\nr = \\frac{81}{243} = \\frac{1}{3}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use this common ratio to find the values of \\( x \\) and \\( y \\):\n\\[\nx = 81 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = 27\n\\]\n\\[\ny = 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{3} = 1\n\\]\n\nNow, we calculate \\( x + y \\):\n\\[\nx + y = 27 + 1 = 28\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\( x + y \\) is \\(\\boxed{28}\\)."
