"To determine the time in Denver when the train arrives, we need to account for the time difference between New York and Denver. The time difference between New York and Denver is 7 hours.\n\nThe train leaves New York at 2 p.m. New York time. Adding the time difference of 7 hours to 2 p.m. New York time gives us:\n\n\\[ 2 \\text{ p.m.} + 7 \\text{ hours} = 9 \\text{ p.m.} \\text{ Denver time} \\]\n\nNext, the train takes 45 hours to travel from New York to Denver. Adding 45 hours to 9 p.m. Denver time gives us:\n\n\\[ 9 \\text{ p.m.} + 45 \\text{ hours} = 6 \\text{ a.m.} \\text{ Denver time} \\]\n\nTherefore, the train arrives in Denver at 6 a.m. Denver time.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is 6 a.m. Denver time."
