"To find the range of the function \\( j(x) = 2x^2 + 1 \\) on the domain \\([-1, 2]\\), we need to determine the values of \\( j(x) \\) for \\( x \\) in this interval.\n\nFirst, we evaluate \\( j(x) \\) at the endpoints of the domain:\n\\[\nj(-1) = 2(-1)^2 + 1 = 2(1) + 1 = 3 + 1 = 4\n\\]\n\\[\nj(2) = 2(2)^2 + 1 = 2(4) + 1 = 8 + 1 = 9\n\\]\n\nThus, the range of \\( j(x) \\) on the domain \\([-1, 2]\\) is the set of all values that \\( j(x) \\) can take, which is the interval \\([4, 9]\\).\n\nTherefore, the range of \\( j(x) \\) is \\(\\boxed{[4, 9]}\\)."
