"To find the constant \\( k \\) that will make \\( y^2 + 24y + 16 + k \\) the square of a binomial, we need to express it in the form \\( (y + a)^2 \\).\n\nFirst, expand \\( (y + a)^2 \\):\n\\[\n(y + a)^2 = y^2 + 2ay + a^2\n\\]\n\nWe need this to match \\( y^2 + 24y + 16 + k \\). Therefore, we equate the coefficients:\n\\[\n2a = 24 \\implies a = 12\n\\]\n\\[\na^2 = 16 + k\n\\]\n\nSubstitute \\( a = 12 \\) into the second equation:\n\\[\n12^2 = 16 + k\n\\]\n\\[\n144 = 16 + k\n\\]\n\\[\n for \\( k \\):\n\\[\nk = 144 - 16 = 128\n\\]\n\nThus, the constant \\( k \\) is \\(\\boxed{128}\\)."
