"Let \\( n \\) be the number of nickels and \\( d \\) be the number of nickels. We have two equations:\n\n1. \\( n + d = 11 \\)\n2. \\( 5n + 10d = 75 \\)\n\nWe can simplify the second equation by dividing everything by 5:\n\n\\[ n + 2d = 15 \\]\n\nNow we have the system of equations:\n\n1. \\( n + d = 11 \\)\n2. \\( n + 2d = 15 \\)\n\nWe can solve this system by subtracting the first equation from the second:\n\n\\[ (n + 2d) - (n + d) = 15 - 11 \\]\n\\[ d = 4 \\]\n\nSo, Hillary has 4 dimes. Now we substitute \\( d = 4 \\) back into the first equation to find \\( n \\):\n\n\\[ n + 4 = 11 \\]\n\\[ n = 7 \\]\n\nTherefore, Hillary has 7 nickels.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $7$. I hope it is correct."
