"The cost to carpet a floor is directly proportional to the area. Therefore, we can set up a proportion to find the cost of the new floor.\n\nThe area of the first floor is \\(14 \\times 5 = 70\\) square feet.\nThe area of the second floor is \\(16 \\times 13 = 208\\) square feet.\n\nLet \\(C\\) be the cost of the second floor. Since the cost is directly proportional to the area, we can write:\n\\[\n\\frac{105}{70} = \\frac{C}{208}\n\\]\n\nSolving for \\(C\\), we get:\n\\[\nC = 105 \\times \\frac{208}{70} = 105 \\times 2.9714285714285714 = 312\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the cost to carpet the floor that is \\(16 \\times 13\\) square feet is \\(\\boxed{312}\\) dollars."
"To find \\( g(4) \\), we need to use the given function \\( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \\).\n\nFirst, we need to find \\( f(4) \\):\n\\[\nf(x) = 2x - 3\n\\]\n\\[\nf(4) = 2(4) - 3 = 8 - 3 = 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we substitute \\( f(4) = 5 \\) into the equation \\( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \\):\n\\[\ng(f(4)) = g(5) = 5 - 4(4) = 5 - 16 = -11\n\\]\n\nTherefore, \\( g(4) = -11 \\).\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is \\(-11\\)."
"To find the value of \\( y \\) when \\( x = -2 \\) for the equation \\( y = 8 - 5x + 4x^2 \\), we substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the equation and simplify.\n\nFirst, substitute \\( x = -2 \\) into the equation:\n\\[ y = 8 - 5(-2) + 4(-2)^2 \\]\n\nNext, calculate each term:\n\\[ -5(-2) = 10 \\]\n\\[ 4(-2)^2 = 4 \\cdot 4 = 16 \\]\n\nNow, substitute these values back into the equation:\n\\[ y = 8 + 10 + 16 \\]\n\nAdd the numbers together:\n\\[ y = 34 \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\( y \\) when \\( x = -2 \\) is \\(\\boxed{34}\\)."
