"Let \\( d \\) be the number of hours David worked. Since Alan worked three times as many hours as David, Alan worked \\( 3d \\) hours.\n\nThe number of bricks placed by David is \\( 30d \\).\nThe number of bricks placed by Alan is \\( 30 \\times 3d = 90d \\).\n\nThe total number of bricks placed by both Alan and David is \\( 30d + 90d = 120d \\).\n\nWe know that the total number of bricks placed is 600, so we set up the equation:\n\\[ 120d = 600 \\]\n\nSolving for \\( d \\):\n\\[ d = \\frac{600}{120} = 5 \\]\n\nTherefore, David worked 5 hours. The number of bricks placed by David is:\n\\[ 30 \\times 5 = 150 \\]\n\nSo, David laid \\(\\boxed{150}\\) bricks."
