"Let $w$ be the number of matches she won before the weekend began. Then her win ratio is $\\frac{w}{w+4}$, and we want this to be greater than $0.503$. We can rewrite this inequality as:\n\n$$\\frac{w}{w+4} > 0.503$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $w+4$, we get:\n\n$$w > 0.503(w+4)$$\n\nExpanding and simplifying, we get:\n\n$$w > 0.503w + 2.012$$\n\nSubtracting $0.503w$ from both sides, we get:\n\n$$0.497w > 2.012$$\n\nDividing both sides by $0.497$, we get:\n\n$$w > 4$$\n\nSince $w$ must be an integer, the largest possible value for $w$ is $5$. Therefore, the largest number of matches she could've won before the weekend began is $\\boxed{5}$."
