"We can solve the system of equations by substitution or elimination. Let's use elimination:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n5x-2y&=7,\\\\\n3x+y&=2.\n\\end{align*}\n\nFirst, we multiply the second equation by 2 to make the coefficients of $y$ the same:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n6x+2y&=4.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we subtract the first equation from this result:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n(6x+2y)-(5x-2y)&=4-7,\\\\\nx&=-3.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNext, we substitute $x=-3$ back into the second equation:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n3(-3)+y&=2,\\\\\ny&=5.\n\\end{align*}\n\nNow, we can compute $24x-14y$:\n\n\\begin{align*}\n24(-3)-14(5)&==-72-70,\\\\\n&=-142.\n\\end{align*}\n\nTherefore, the answer is $\\boxed{-142}$."
