"To find the $x$-intercept of the line containing the points $(7,4)$ and $(6, 3)$, we need to determine the $x$-coordinate when $y = 0$.\n\nFirst, we find the slope of the line using the slope formula:\n$$m = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1} = \\frac{3 - 4}{6 - 7} = -1$$\n\nNext, we use the point-slope form of the equation of a line:\n$$y - y_1 = m(x - x_1)$$\nUsing the point $(7, 4)$ and the slope $m = -1$:\n$$y - 4 = -1(x - 7)$$\n$$y = -x + 11$$\n\nTo find the $x$-intercept, we set $y = 0$ and solve for $x$:\n$$0 = -x + 11$$\n$$x = 11$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the $x$-intercept is $\\boxed{11}$."
"To expand the expression \\((x+3)(2x-6)\\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):\n\n1. First, multiply the first terms in each binomial:\n   \\[\n   x \\cdot 2x = 2x^2\n   \\]\n\n2. Next, multiply the outer terms in each binomial:\n   \\[\n   x \\cdot (-6) = -6x\n   \\]\n\n3. Then, multiply the inner terms in each binomial:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot 2x = 6x\n   \\]\n\n4. Finally, multiply the last terms in each binomial:\n   \\[\n   3 \\cdot (-6) = -18\n   \\]\n\nNow, combine all these results together:\n\\[\n2x^2 - 6x + 6x - 18\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n2x^2 + 0x - 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the expanded form of the expression is:\n\\[\nboxed{2x^2 - 18}\n\\]"
"First, we need to find the ceiling of $\\sqrt{20}\\). The ceiling function \\(\\lceil x \\rceil\\) gives the smallest integer greater than or equal to \\(x\\).\n\n\\[\n\\sqrt{20} \\approx 4.472\n\\]\n\nThe smallest integer greater than or equal to 4.472 is 5. Therefore,\n\n\\[\n\\lceil \\sqrt{20} \\rceil = 5\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to square this value:\n\n\\[\n\\lceil \\sqrt{20} \\rceil^2 = 5^2 = 25\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25}\n\\]"
"The arithmetic mean of $A$, $B$, and $C$ is given by 10. Therefore, we can write\n\n$$\\frac{A + B + C}{3} = 10.$$\n\nWe are also given that $A = B - 6$ and $C = B + 3$. Substituting these into the equation, we get:\n\n$$\\frac{(B - 6) + B + (B + 3)}{3} = 10.$$\n\nSimplifying the numerator, we have:\n\n$$\\frac{3B - 3}{3} = 10.$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by 3, we get:\n\n$$3B - 3 = 30.$$\n\nAdding 3 to both sides, we get:\n\n$$3B = 33.$$\n\nDividing by 3, we get we get:\n\n$$B = 11.$$\n\nNow, we can find $C$:\n\n$$C = B + 3 = 11 + 3 = 14.$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $C$ is:\n\n$$\\boxed{14}.$$"
"To determine how many pints of water Jasmine would drink in the next 10 miles, we first need to find her rate of water consumption per mile.\n\nJasmine drank 1.5 pints of water in the first 3 miles. Therefore, her rate of water consumption per mile is:\n\\[\n\\frac{1.5 \\text{ pints}}{3 \\text{ miles}} = 0.5 \\text{ pints per mile}\n\\]\n\nNext, we use this rate to calculate the amount of water she would drink in the next 10 miles:\n\\[\n0.5 \\text{ pints per mile} \\times 10 \\text{ miles} = 5 \\text{ pints}\n\\]\n\nThus, Jasmine would drink \\boxed{5} pints of water in the next 10 miles."
