"To find the value of the expression \\(\\frac{4x^2}{9y^2}\\) given \\(x = 3\\) and \\(y = 2\\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. Substitute the given values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\) into the expression.\n2. Simplify the expression.\n\nFirst, substitute \\(x = 3\\) and \\(y = 2\\) into the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{4x^2}{9y^2} = \\frac{4(3)^2}{9(2)^2}\n\\]\n\nNext, calculate the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n4(3)^2 = 4 \\cdot 9 = 36\n\\]\n\\[\n9(2)^2 = 9 \\cdot 4 = 36\n\\]\n\nNow, divide the numerator by the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{36}{36} = 1\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the value of the expression is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
