"To find the minimum value of the function \\( y = x^2 - 7 \\), we need to determine the vertex of the parabola represented by this equation. The general form of a parabola is \\( y = ax^2 + bx + c \\), where \\( a = 1 \\), \\( b = 0 \\), and \\( c = -7 \\).\n\nThe vertex of a parabola \\( y = ax^2 + bx + c \\) occurs at \\( x = -\\frac{b}{2a} \\). Here, \\( b = 0 \\) and \\( a = 1 \\), so the vertex occurs at \\( x = 0 \\).\n\nSubstituting \\( x = 0 \\) into the equation \\( y = x^2 - 7 \\), we get:\n\n\\[ y = 0^2 - 7 = -7 \\]\n\nTherefore, the minimum value of \\( y \\) is \\(\\boxed{-7}\\)."
