"To find the number of ways to choose a 3-person committee from a group of 8 people, we use the combination formula \\( \\binom{n}{k} = \\frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!} \\), where \\( n \\) is the total number of people and \\( k \\) is the number of people to choose.\n\nHere, \\( n = 8 \\) and \\( k = 3 \\).\n\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{3} = \\frac{8!}{3!(8-3)!} = \\frac{8!}{3! \\cdot 5!}\n\\]\n\nWe can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n\\[\n\\binom{8}{3} = \\frac{8 \\times 7 \\times 6}{3 \\times 2 \\times 1} = \\frac{336}{6} = 56\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of ways to choose a 3-person committee from a group of 8 people is \\(\\boxed{56}\\)."
