"We can simplify the expression $\\frac{18!}{16!}$ by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator.\n\nFirst, let's write out the factorials:\n\n$18! = 18 \\times 17 \\times 16 \\times \\cdots \\times 2 \\times 1$\n\n$16! = 16 \\times 15 \\times 14 \\times \\cdots \\times 2 \\times 1$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the expression as:\n\n$\\frac{18!}{16!} = \\frac{18 \\times 17 \\times 16 \\times \\cdots \\times 2 \\times 1}{16 \\times 15 \\times 14 \\times \\cdots \\times 2 \\times 1}$\n\nNext, we can cancel out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$\\frac{18!}{16!} = 18$\n\nTherefore, the simplified expression is $\\boxed{18}$."
