"To determine the number of ways to choose the officers, secretary, and treasurer from a club of 25 members, where individual members can hold up to 2 offices but not all 3 offices, we need to consider the following:\n\n1. **Choosing the President**: There are 25 possible choices for the president.\n2. **Choosing the Secretary**: After choosing the president, there are 24 remaining members to choose from for the secretary.\n3. **Choosing the Treasurer**: After choosing the president and the secretary, there are 23 remaining members to choose from for the treasurer.\n\nThe total number of ways to choose the officers is the product of the number of choices for each position:\n\n\\[\n25 \\times 24 \\times 23\n\\]\n\nCalculating this product:\n\n\\[\n25 \\times 24 = 600\n\\]\n\\[\n600 \\times 23 = 13800\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of ways to choose the officers is \\(\\boxed{13800}\\)."
