"Let's denote the number of slices that have both pepperoni and mushrooms as \\( x \\).\n\nWe know the following:\n- The total number of slices is 12.\n- The number of slices with only pepperoni is 5.\n- The number of slices with mushrooms is 8.\n\nSince every slice has at least one topping, we can use the principle of inclusion-exclusion to find the number of slices with both toppings.\n\nThe total number of slices can be expressed as:\n\\[ \\text{Total slices} = \\text{Slices with only pepperoni} + \\text{Slices with mushrooms} - \\text{Slices with both toppings} \\]\n\nSubstituting the given values:\n\\[ 12 = 5 + 8 - x \\]\n\nSolving for \\( x \\):\n\\[ 12 = 13 - x \\]\n\\[ x = 13 - 12 \\]\n\\[ x = 1 \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of slices that have both pepperoni and mushrooms is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
