"The area of an isosceles trapezoid can be calculated using the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (\\text{Base}_1 + \\text{Base}_2) \\times \\text{Height}\n\\]\n\nGiven:\n- Base 1 = 7 units\n- Base 2 = 17 units\n- Height (leg) = 13 units\n\nSubstitute these values into the formula:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times (7 + 17) \\times 13\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\frac{1}{2} \\times 24 \\times 13\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 12 \\times 13\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = 156\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the isosceles trapezoid is \\boxed{156} square units."
