"Let $n$ be the number of sides of the polygon. The measure of an exterior angle is $\\frac{360^\\circ}{n}$, and the measure of an interior angle is $180^\\circ - \\frac{360^\\circ}{n}$. According to the problem, we have\n\n$$180^\\circ - \\frac{360^\\circ}{n} = 6.5 \\cdot \\frac{360^\\circ}{n}.$$\n\nSimplifying the equation, we get\n\n$$180^\\circ - \\frac{360^\\circ}{n} = 204^\\circ.$$\n\nRearranging the terms, we get\n\n$$\\frac{360^\\circ}{n} = 24^\\circ.$$\n\nSolving for $n$, we get\n\n$$n = \\frac{360^\\circ}{24^\\circ} = 15.$$\n\nTherefore, the polygon has $\\boxed{15}$ sides."
