"To determine the number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with, we need to consider the options available for each component of the Mr. Potato Head's personality.\n\n1. **Hairstyles**: There are 3 hairstyles.\n2. **Eyebrows**: There are 2 sets of eyebrows.\n3. **Eyes**: There is 1 pair of googly eyes.\n4. **Ears**: There are 2 sets of ears.\n5. **Lips**: There are 2 sets of lips.\n6. **Shoes**: There are 2 options (regular shoes and clown shoes).\n\nSince Mr. Potato Head can be bald, there are no options for the hair.\n\nTo find the total number of different personalities, we multiply the number of options for each component:\n\n\\[\n3 \\text{ hairstyles} \\times 2 \\text{ eyebrows} \\times 1 \\text{ eyes} \\times 2 \\text{ ears} \\times 2 \\text{ lips} \\times 2 \\text{ shoes} = 24\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the number of different wacky personalities Tom can come up with is \\(\\boxed{24}\\)."
