"Let $M$ be the number of students participating in MATHCOUNTS, $S$ be the number of students participating in science club, and $B$ be the number of students participating in both MATHCOUNTS and science club. We know that $M = 28$, $S = 21$, and the total number of students is 50. Also, 6 students participate in neither, so the number of students participating in at least one of the clubs is $50 - 6 = 44$.\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion-exclusion, we have:\n\n$$M + S - B = 44$$\n\nSubstituting the known values, we get:\n\n$$28 + 21 - B = 44$$\n\nSolving for $B$, we get:\n\n$$49 - B = 44$$\n\n$$B = 5$$\n\nTherefore, the number of students participating in both MATHCOUNTS and science club is $\\boxed{5}$."
