"Let \\( n \\) be the number of tests Brian took before his last test. The sum of his test scores before the last test is \\( 91n \\).\n\nAfter he scores 98 on his last test, the new sum of his test scores becomes \\( 91n + 98 \\).\n\nThe new arithmetic mean is given as 92, so the new sum of his test scores is also \\( 92(n + 1) \\).\n\nSetting up the equation:\n\\[ 91n + 98 = 92(n + 1) \\]\n\nExpanding and simplifying:\n\\[ 91n + 98 = 92n + 92 \\]\n\\[ 98 - 92 = 92n - 91n \\]\n\\[ 6 = n \\ \\]\n\\[ n = 6 \\]\n\nTherefore, Brian took 6 tests before his last test. Including the last test, he took a total of \\( 6 + 1 = 7 \\) tests.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $7$."
