"We can use the Law of Cosines to find the length of $\\overline{BC}$. The Law of Cosines states that for any triangle $ABC$,\n\n$$BC^2 = AB^2 + AC^2 - 2AB \\cos \\angle A.$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get\n\n$$BC^2 = 20^2 + 20^2 - 2 \\cdot 20 \\cdot 20 \\cdot \\cos 30^\\circ.$$\n\nSimplifying, we have\n\n$$BC^2 = 400 + 400 - 800 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} = 800 - 400 = 400.$$\n\nTaking the square root of both sides, we get\n\n$$BC = \\sqrt{400} = 20.$$\n\nTherefore, the length of $\\overline{BC}$ is $\\boxed{20}$ cm."
"The mean of the set $\\{6, x, 22\\}$ is $\\frac{6 + x + 22}{3}$. The median of the set is $x$. Setting the mean equal to the median, we have:\n\n$$\\frac{6 + x + 22}{3} = x$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by 3, we get:\n\n$$6 + x + 22 = 3x$$\n\nSubtracting $x$ from both sides, we get:\n\n$$6 + 22 = 2x$$\n\nSubtracting 6 from both sides, we get:\n\n$$22 = 2x$$\n\nDividing both sides by 2, we get:\n\n$$x = 11$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $x$ is $\\boxed{11}$."
