"To find the perimeter of hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\), we need to sum the lengths of all its sides. The hexagon is formed by arranging 48 congruent paralleramsrams in a chevron pattern. Each parallelogram has sides of length 62 feet and 20 feet.\n\nFirst, let's identify the lengths of the sides of the hexagon:\n- Side \\(AB\\) is 20 feet.\n- Side \\(BC\\) is 62 feet.\n- Side \\(CD\\) is 20 feet.\n- Side \\(DE\\) is 62 feet.\n- Side \\(EF\\) is 20 feet.\n- Side \\(FA\\) is 62 feet.\n\nNext, we sum these lengths to find the perimeter:\n\\[\n20 + 62 + 20 + 62 + 20 + 62 = 246 \\text{ feet}\n\\]\n\nThus, the perimeter of hexagon \\(ABCDEF\\) is \\(\\boxed{246}\\) feet."
