"The circumference of a circle is given by the formula \\( C = 2\\pi r \\), where \\( C \\) is the circumference and \\( r \\) is the radius. Given that the circumference is \\( 8\\pi \\) units, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 8\\pi = 2\\pi r \\]\n\nTo find the radius \\( r \\), we divide both sides of the equation by \\( 2\\pi \\):\n\n\\[ r = \\frac{8\\pi}{2\\pi} = 4 \\]\n\nThe area of a circle is given by the formula \\( A = \\pi r^2 \\). Substituting the radius \\( r = 4 \\) into the formula, we get:\n\n\\[ A = \\pi (4)^2 = 16\\pi \\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the circle is \\(\\boxed{16\\pi}\\) square units."
