"The area of a circle is given by the formula \\( A = \\pi r^2 \\), where \\( r \\) is the radius.\n\nFirst, we calculate  the area of the circle with radius 2 inches:\n\\[ A = \\pi (2)^2 = 4\\pi \\]\n\nWhen the radius is doubled, the new radius becomes \\( 2 \\times 2 = 4 \\) inches.\n\nNext, we calculate the area of the circle with radius 4 inches:\n\\[ A = \\pi (4)^2 = 16\\pi \\]\n\nThe increase in area is the difference between the new area and the original area:\n\\[ \\text{Increase in area} = 16\\pi - 4\\pi = 12\\pi \\]\n\nTherefore, the area is increased by \\(\\boxed{12\\pi}\\) square inches."
