"To find the least number of days before all three students will report to the principal on the same day, we need to determine the least common multiple (LCM) of their reporting intervals.\n\nFirst, we find the prime factorizations of each interval:\n- Rachel: \\(9 = 3^2\\)\n- Jessica: \\(12 = 2^2 \\times 3\\)\n- Richard: \\(15 = 3 \\times 5\\)\n\nThe LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:\n- The highest power of \\(2\\) is \\(2^2\\).\n- The highest power of \\(3\\) is \\(3^2\\).\n- The highest power of \\(5\\) is \\(5\\).\n\nPutting these together, we get:\n\\[\n\\text{LCM} = 2^2 \\times 3^2 \\times 5 = 4 \\times 9 \\times 5 = 180\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the least number of days before all three students will report to the principal on the same day is \\(\\boxed{180}\\)."
