"Let the side length of each square be \\( s \\). Since three squares are placed side by side, the length of the rectangle is \\( 3s \\) and the width is \\( s \\).\n\nThe perimeter of the rectangle is given by the formula:\n\\[\n\\text{Perimeter} = 2 \\times (\\text{length} + \\text{width})\n\\]\nSubstituting the given dimensions:\n\\[\n104 = 2 \\times (3s + s)\n\\]\n\\[\n104 = 2 \\times 4s\n\\]\n\\[\n104 = 8s\n\\]\n\\[\ns = \\frac{104}{8}\n\\]\n\\[\ns = 13\n\\]\n\nThe area of each square is:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = s^2 = 13^2 = 169\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of each square is \\(\\boxed{169}\\) square inches."
