"The sum of the numbers in each row, column, and diagonal must be equal. Let's calculate the sum of the first row:\n\n$$(n-3) + 3 + (n+1) = 3n - 1$$\n\nSince the square is a magic square, the sum of the second row must also be $3n - 1$:\n\n$$(n+2) + (2n-9) + 1 = 3n - 1$$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n$$3n - 6 = 3n - 1$$\n\nThis equation is always true, so we need to find the sum of the third row:\n\n$$2 + n + (n-1) = 3n - 1$$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n$$2 + n - 1 = 3n - 1$$\n\nSolving for $n$, we get:\n$$2 = 2n$$\n$$n = 1$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $n$ is $\\boxed{1}$."
