"We need to find the first odd-numbered year after $2006$ that has the property that when split after the third digit into a three-digit integer and a one-digit integer, the two integers have a common factor greater than one.\n\nLet's consider the year $2007$:\n- Split $2007$ after the third digit: $200$ and $7$.\n- Check if $200$ and $7$ have a common factor greater than one:\n  - The prime factorization of $200$ is $2^2 \\times 5^2$.\n  - The prime factorization of $7$ is $7$.\n  - The common prime factor is $7$.\n\nSince $200$ and $7$ have a common factor greater than one, the year $2007$ satisfies the condition.\n\nTherefore, the first odd-numbered year after $2006$ that has this property is $\\boxed{2007}$."
