"To find the perimeter of \\(\\triangle PQS\\), we need to sum the lengths of all its sides. The sides of the triangle are given as follows:\n\n- \\(PQ = 5\\)\n- \\(QS = 13\\)\n- \\(PS = 37\\)\n\nThe perimeter \\(P\\) of \\(\\triangle PQS\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\nP = PQ + QS + PS\n\\]\n\nSubstituting the given side lengths:\n\n\\[\nP = 5 + 13 + 37\n\\]\n\nAdding these together:\n\n\\[\nP = 55\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of \\(\\triangle PQS\\) is \\(\\boxed{55}\\)."
