"To solve the equation \\(5x - 3 = 12\\), we first isolate \\(x\\):\n\n1. Add 3 to both sides:\n   \\[\n   5x - 3 + 3 = 12 + 3\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   5x = 15\n   \\]\n\n2. Divide both sides by 5:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{5x}{5} = \\frac{15}{5}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 3\n   \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the value of \\(5x + 3\\):\n\n1. Substitute \\(x = 3\\) into the expression \\(5x + 3\\):\n   \\[\n   5(3) + 3 = 15 + 3 = 18\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the value of \\(5x + 3\\) is \\(\\boxed{18}\\)."
