"First, we need to find the radius of the circle. The circumference of a circle is given by the formula \\( C = 2\\pi r \\), where \\( r \\) is the radius and \\( C \\) is the circumference. Given that the circumference is \\( 12\\pi \\) units, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ 2\\pi r = 12\\pi \\]\n\nSolving for \\( r \\), we get both sides by \\( r \\):\n\n\\[ 2r = 12 \\]\n\\[ r = 6 \\]\n\nSo, the radius of the circle is 6 units. Since the side of the square is the same as the radius of the circle, the side of the square is also 6 units.\n\nThe area of a square is given by the formula \\( \\text{Area} = \\text{side}^2 \\). Therefore, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[ \\text{Area} = 6^2 = 36 \\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is \\(\\boxed{36}\\) square units."
