"To simplify \\(\\frac{91}{26}\\), we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 91 and 26 and divide both the numerator and the denominator by this GCD.\n\nFirst, let's find the prime factorization of 91 and 26:\n\n\\[\n91 = 7 \\times 13\n\\]\n\\[\n26 = 2 \\times 13\n\\]\n\nThe common prime factor between 91 and 26 is 13. Therefore, the GCD of 91 and 26 is 13.\n\nNow, we divide both the numerator and the denominator by the GCD:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{91 \\div 13}{26 \\div 13} = \\frac{7}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the simplified form of \\(\\frac{91}{26}\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{7}{2}}\\)."
