"To find the area of the region of overlap, we need to determine the dimensions of the overlapping region. The overlapping region is a rectangle that is common to both sheets of paper.\n\nThe dimensions of the first sheet of paper are 8 inches by 10 inches.\nThe dimensions of the second sheet of paper are 8.5 inches by 11 inches.\n\nThe width of the overlapping region is the minimum of the widths of the two sheets, which is 8.5 inches.\nThe height of the overlapping region is the minimum of the heights of the two sheets, which is 8 inches.\n\nThe area of the overlapping region is given by the product of its width and height:\n\\[\n\\text{Area} = \\text{width} \\times \\text{height} = 8.5 \\text{ inches} \\times 8 \\text{ inches} = 68 \\text{ square inches}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the region of overlap is \\boxed{68} square inches."
