"Let's determine the cost of each type of fruit in terms of \\( x \\):\n\n1. Dragonfruit costs \\( x - 4 \\) dollars.\n2. Rambutan costs \\( 2x \\) dollars more than dragonfruit, so it costs \\( 2x - 4 \\) dollars.\n3. Starfruit is five dollars less expensive than rambutan, so it costs \\( (2x - 4) - 5 = x - 9 \\) dollars.\n\nNow, we need to find the total cost of one rambutan, two starfruit, and three dragonfruit:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost} = (2x - 4) + 2(x - 9) + 3(x - 4)\n\\]\n\nSimplify the expression:\n\n\\[\n\\text{Total cost} = 2x - 4 + 2x - 18 + 3x - 12 = 7x - 34\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total cost is \\(\\boxed{7x - 34}\\) dollars."
