"To find the greatest common factor (GCF) of 99 and 100, we can use the Euclidean algorithm. The Euclidean algorithm involves repeated division and taking remainders until we reach a remainder of 0.\n\n1. Divide 100 by 99 and find the remainder:\n   \\[\n   100 \\div 99 = 1 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 1\n   \\]\n\n2. Now, divide 99 by the remainder from the previous step:\n   \\[\n   99 \\div 1 = 99 \\quad \\text{remainder} \\quad 0\n   \\]\n\nSince the remainder is now 0, we stop here. The last non-zero remainder is 1.\n\nTherefore, the greatest common factor of 99 and 100 is \\(\\boxed{1}\\)."
