"To determine how many degrees the temperature will rise in the next 2 hours, we first need to find the rate of temperature increase per minute. We know that the temperature rises by 1.5 degrees in 15 minutes. Therefore, the rate of temperature increase per minute is:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1.5 \\text{ degrees}}{15 \\text{ minutes}} = 0.10 \\text{ degrees per minute}\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to calculate the total increase in minutes over 2 hours. Since there are 60 minutes in an hour, we have:\n\n\\[\n2 \\text{ hours} \\times 60 \\text{ minutes per hour} = 120 \\text{ minutes}\n\\]\n\nNow, we multiply the rate of temperature increase per minute by the total number of minutes:\n\n\\[\n0.10 \\text{ degrees per minute} \\times 120 \\text{ minutes} = 12 \\text{ degrees}\n\\]\n\nThus, the temperature will rise by \\boxed{12} degrees in the next 2 hours."
"To determine the tax for a house assessed at \\$160,000, we first need to find the tax rate. The tax rate is the tax paid divided by the assessed value of the house.\n\nGiven:\n- A house assessed at \\$120,000 that pays \\$3,000 in taxes.\n\nThe tax rate is:\n\\[\n\\text{Tax rate} = \\frac{\\text{Tax paid}}{\\text{Assessed value}} = \\frac{3,000}{120,000} = 0.025\n\\]\n\nNow, we use this tax rate to find the tax for a house assessed at \\$160,000:\n\\[\n\\text{Tax} = \\text{Tax rate} \\times \\text{Assessed value} = 0.025 \\times 160,000 = 4,000\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the tax for a house assessed at \\$160,000 is \\boxed{4000}.\n\nFinal Answer: The final answer is $4000$. I hope it is correct."
