"To determine the number of handshakes that take place between the six members of the Skateer University hockey team and the six members of the Iceburg Tech team, we can use the concept of combinations. Each handshake involves two members from different teams.\n\nFirst, we calculate the number of ways to choose 2 members from the Skateer University team:\n\\[\n\\binom{6}{2} = \\frac{6 \\times 5}{2 \\times 1} = 15\n\\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of ways to choose 2 members from the Iceburg Tech team:\n\\[\n\\binom{6}{2} = \\frac{6 \\times 5}{2 \\times 1} = 15\n\\]\n\nSince each handshake involves one member from each team, we multiply the number of ways to choose 2 members from each team:\n\\[\n15 \\times 15 = 225\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of handshakes that take place is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{225}\n\\]"
