"We can use the principle of inclusion and exclusion to find the number of students taking both history and science. Let $H$ be the set of students taking history and $S$ be the set of students taking science. We know that $|H| = 126$, $|S| = 129$, and $|H \\cup S| = 200$. We want to find $|H \\cap S|$.\n\nUsing the principle of inclusion and exclusion, we have:\n\n$$|H \\cup S| = |H| + |S| - |H \\cap S|$$\n\nSubstituting the given values, we get:\n\n$$200 = 126 + 129 - |H \\cap S|$$\n\nSolving for $|H \\cap S|$, we get:\n\n$$|H \\cap S| = 255 - 200 = 55$$\n\nTherefore, the number of students taking both history and science is $\\boxed{55}$."
