"To determine how many more ice cream cones Izzy can sell, we need to divide the total amount of ice cream left by the amount of ice cream each cone contains.\n\nGiven:\n- Izzy has \\(\\frac{3}{4}\\) of a gallon of ice cream left.\n- Each ice cream cone contains \\(\\frac{1}{32}\\) of a gallon of ice cream.\n\nWe need to calculate:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{4} \\div \\frac{1}{32}\n\\]\n\nTo divide by a fraction, we multiply by its reciprocal:\n\\[\n\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{32}{1} = \\frac{3 \\times 32}{4 \\times 1} = \\frac{96}{4} = 24\n\\]\n\nTherefore, Izzy can sell \\(\\boxed{24}\\) more ice cream cones."
