"To find the actual distance between the two cities, we need to use the scale given on the map. The scale is 0.5 cm:1 km, which means that every 0.5 cm on the map represents 1 km in reality.\n\nThe distance between the two cities on the map is 4 centimeters. We can set up a proportion to find the actual distance:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{0.5 \\text{ cm}}{1 \\text{ km}} = \\frac{4 \\text{ cm}}{x \\text{ km}}\n\\]\n\nTo solve for \\( x \\), we can cross-multiply:\n\n\\[\n0.5 \\cdot x = 4 \\cdot 1\n\\]\n\n\\[\n0.5x = 4\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = \\frac{4}{0.5}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx = 8\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the actual distance between the two cities is \\(\\boxed{8}\\) kilometers."
