"We can use the angle addition formula for cosine and the angle subtraction formula for sine to rewrite the given equation:\n\n$$\\cos (\\alpha + \\beta) + \\sin (\\alpha - \\beta) = \\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta + \\sin \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\cos \\alpha \\sin \\beta = 0.$$\n\nSimplifying, we get:\n\n$$\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta - \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta = 0.$$\n\nThis implies that:\n\n$$\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta = \\sin \\alpha \\sin \\beta.$$\n\nDividing both sides by $\\cos \\alpha \\cos \\beta$, we get:\n\n$$\\tan \\alpha = \\tan \\beta.$$\n\nSince $\\tan \\beta = \\frac{1}{2000}$, we have:\n\n$$\\tan \\alpha = \\frac{1}{2000}.$$\n\nTherefore, the value of $\\tan \\alpha$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2000}}$."
